54 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423243 13194139534500 17592186045417 true] [17592186423254 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423244 13194139534500 17592186045417 true] [17592186423254 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423249 13194139534500 17592186045417 true] [17592186423254 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423250 13194139534500 17592186045417 true] [17592186423254 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423252 13194139534500 17592186045417 true] [17592186423254 1069 "q-341778" 13194139534500 17592186045417 true] [17592186423254 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534500 17592186045417 true] [17592186423254 1071 "Let $f(x)$ be the $2L$-periodic extension of a function $F(x)$ from $x\\in [-L,L)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({{field-1}})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({{field-2}}).\n$$\n\nThe $6$th sine coefficient of the series is\n\n$$\n{b}_{6}={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $F(x)={x}^{3}$ and $L=3,$ the $6$th sine coefficient becomes\n\n$$\n{b}_{6}={{field-4}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-5}}.\n$$" 13194139534500 17592186045417 true] [17592186423254 1072 #uuid "4886c497-1cb0-54c5-b33a-8a4433090897" 13194139534500 17592186045417 true] [17592186423254 1074 "Recall that multiplying the argument of a function by $k\\ne 0$ represents the horizontal stretching of the corresponding graph by a factor of $\\frac{1}{k}.$\n\nNow, let $s=\\frac{\\pi }{L}x.$ Then, since $f(x)$ has a period of $2L,$ the function\n\n$$\ng(s)=f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }s)\n$$\n\nmust have a period of $2L\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}=2\\pi .$ \n\nThe Fourier series of $g(s)$ is\n\n$$\ng(s)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(ns)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(ns),\n$$\n\nwhere:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\ {a}_{n} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(ns)\\,\\text{d}s,\\,n\\ge 1 \\\\ {b}_{n} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(ns)\\,\\text{d}s,\\,n\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $s=\\frac{\\pi }{L}x$ and using the fact that $g(s)=f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }s),$ we get the Fourier series of $f(x):$\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)\n$$\n\nTherefore, $6$th sine coefficient of $f(x)$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{6} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }s)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}(\\frac{\\pi }{L}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{6\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{6\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $L=3$ and $f(x)={x}^{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{6} & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{6\\pi }{3}x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {\\int }_{-3}^{3}{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534500 17592186045417 true] [17592186423255 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423245 13194139534500 17592186045417 true] [17592186423255 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423246 13194139534500 17592186045417 true] [17592186423255 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423247 13194139534500 17592186045417 true] [17592186423255 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423248 13194139534500 17592186045417 true] [17592186423255 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423253 13194139534500 17592186045417 true] [17592186423255 1069 "q-341785" 13194139534500 17592186045417 true] [17592186423255 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534500 17592186045417 true] [17592186423255 1071 "Let $f(x)$ be the $2L$-periodic extension of a function $F(x)$ from $x\\in [-L,L)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({{field-1}})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({{field-2}}).\n$$\n\nThe constant coefficient of the series is\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $F(x)={cos}^{2}⁡(x)$ and $L=4,$ the constant coefficient becomes\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}={{field-4}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-5}}.\n$$" 13194139534500 17592186045417 true] [17592186423255 1072 #uuid "d180264d-6aaf-5aca-a8a3-12aea15eb407" 13194139534500 17592186045417 true] [17592186423255 1074 "Recall that multiplying the argument of a function by $k\\ne 0$ represents the horizontal stretching of the corresponding graph by a factor of $\\frac{1}{k}.$\n\nNow, let $s=\\frac{\\pi }{L}x.$ Then, since $f(x)$ has a period of $2L,$ the function\n\n$$\ng(s)=f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }s)\n$$\n\nmust have a period of $2L\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}=2\\pi .$ \n\nThe Fourier series of $g(s)$ is\n\n$$\ng(s)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(ns)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(ns),\n$$\n\nwhere:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\ {a}_{n} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(ns)\\,\\text{d}s,\\,n\\ge 1 \\\\ {b}_{n} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(ns)\\,\\text{d}s,\\,n\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $s=\\frac{\\pi }{L}x$ and using the fact that $g(s)=f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }s),$ we get the Fourier series of $f(x):$\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the constant term of $f(x)$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}(\\frac{\\pi }{L}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $L=4$ and $f(x)={cos}^{2}⁡(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {\\int }_{-4}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534500 17592186045417 true] [17592186423256 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423251 13194139534500 17592186045417 true] [17592186423256 1069 "q-341817" 13194139534500 17592186045417 true] [17592186423256 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534500 17592186045417 true] [17592186423256 1071 "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\n$$\n\nThe Fourier series of the $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of the function \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-2, & x\\in [0,\\pi ) \\\\ 3, & x\\in [-\\pi ,0)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis shown above. Find the exact value of ${a}_{4}.$\n\n${a}_{4}=$ {{field-1}}" 13194139534500 17592186045417 true] [17592186423256 1072 #uuid "fc8861f3-8c91-59c6-b70f-78e5364379e8" 13194139534500 17592186045417 true] [17592186423256 1074 "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the cosine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=\\pi .$ Also, $f(x)=-2$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi )$ and $f(x)=3$ for $x\\in [-\\pi ,0).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{4} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{0}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(-2)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)]}_{-\\pi }^{0}-\\frac{2}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)]}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-4\\pi ))-\\frac{1}{2\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534500 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-00561c08-ad3b-5d9b-ac8d-d1c849b75bfa" 17592186423194 "answer-0123e789-200e-5356-9457-fcfe3958ad6e" 17592186423195 "answer-186b12e8-0537-5623-ab6f-d5dfb2e0cdcc" 17592186423196 "answer-268a6a72-c6bb-5269-8709-c6c7da175bb4" 17592186423197 "answer-282319fc-9f02-5762-9c82-02e738760f50" 17592186423198 "answer-2922dcf4-46a6-5e52-9fe3-e574cf0d2c19" 17592186423199 "answer-2e50c090-e2ce-5c63-a2c9-146ede30820c" 17592186423200 "answer-2efa14e1-1baa-5b6a-aca2-16ad73854b7f" 17592186423201 "answer-302071a9-c016-5db4-bb05-23cc63f79b77" 17592186423202 "answer-330555a3-3265-5f64-bc94-45b597110cad" 17592186423203 "answer-3c31f1c7-dc62-5f6e-ae3f-6593541f6c1e" 17592186423204 "answer-3cff769f-32ca-5374-b8b5-d0b8e71247e0" 17592186423205 "answer-45dd921e-846a-5eef-bdba-5c2ce78f3846" 17592186423206 "answer-477216e7-29ff-535c-919b-7c0025478625" 17592186423207 "answer-4d7363a2-f6fb-591f-8bc8-86df8ca571e5" 17592186423208 "answer-4e94721c-9801-5a97-a7fe-871db3f9b6da" 17592186423209 "answer-541c2cbf-9b2c-5091-88fa-4b3a5ac3c8c0" 17592186423210 "answer-54418102-6b8b-568d-af36-78826b8dc610" 17592186423211 "answer-5af7a6f0-0077-5043-a558-dd52db115cb0" 17592186423212 "answer-5ddc8995-f47b-5b1d-ab95-02eb09995ed1" 17592186423213 "answer-6b54c63d-6367-5121-8b46-fa32b2d6365f" 17592186423214 "answer-6ca8a579-ff53-5300-90a1-e3d79fe3860b" 17592186423215 "answer-6d595da7-7f84-516d-b628-aa452ca2b722" 17592186423216 "answer-6eff947c-8bb4-5509-893e-1e1e8987a8c6" 17592186423217 "answer-736d59ea-f33a-5ef5-b1fc-b2bef5e99802" 17592186423218 "answer-73ee4e81-95a1-562c-b139-d8c63a070d9c" 17592186423219 "answer-80e6e5a7-fe8b-50b6-aad5-976b789e96de" 17592186423220 "an